<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banyuwangi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Banyuwangi is a regency and town at the eastern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, facing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a> across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali-strait">Bali Strait</a>. It covers much of the territory of the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blambangan">Blambangan</a>, which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> conquered in the 1760s and 1770s. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osing-people">Osing people</a> keep a distinct language and culture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/banyuwangi.jpg" alt="Banyuwangi" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Aryphrase at Indonesian Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stasiun-banyuwangi-kota.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
